                <pb facs="0347" n="245" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg245"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.24/656: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morrow</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-12-24T12:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 24,
                                1927—noon</hi>.</date><lb/>[Received 3:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>455. Department’s 304, dated December 21. In my opinion now would be the
                    opportune time to relax the present restrictions on the exportation of
                    airplanes, munitions, and other supplies purchased by the Government of
                    Mexico.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morrow</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
